Three points on this:

1) Every message the game gives you has meaning.  Some are
extremely routine like "The orc swings her orcish dagger.  She
misses!".  Others are extremely NOT routine like "You feel
feverish".  When you encounter a non-routine message it is
important that you have an idea of why it happened.  The reason
you're turning back and forth between a werejackal and a
jackalware is you were bitten by a warejackal or jackalware and
you got the message "You feel feverish".

2) There are advantages to being a ware-critter, and there are
disadvantages to it.  There are also an assortment of ways
to cure it.  None of these are particularly major spoilers.

3) The chances of a bite succeeding so you get the "You feel
feverish" message are highly dependent on the types of armor
you wear.  With armor you can easily tell the AC class and
enchantment because your AC number changes when you put
a piece on or take it off.  But there are other effects that armor
has.  The least spoilly is - weight matters and armor is not
weightless.  The more spoilly aspects have to do with how
armor effects bites or other types of attacks.


